{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux","id":1350157,"title":"The Limits of Flux","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-21T18:04:51-08:00","id":1350157,"title":"The Limits of Flux","content":"Conceptually what should be the limits of Flux? As we try to add other Flux users to Talents we come up with ideas like Wuxia martial arts and even Exalt style types.. Time Lords even Highlander style immortals.. but what should Flux ultimately be allowed to do and not do? Right now it nudges the universe in subtle ways and allows Mercer to Travel through time(and in previous editions to control its flow).<br /> <br /> I mean given direct conscious control of say Dramatic editing you'd have full on reality manipulators but... that seems to step heavily on the toes of Eximorph concepts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T00:55:23-08:00","id":1350204,"title":"","content":"I'd stop short of full-on reality manipulation. That said, stepping on toes shouldn't be as much of a concern. Except for specific effects like the Telepathy and Clairsentience Aptitudes, Novas can do anything Psions/Psiads can do. With Mega-Attributes, they can generally do it much better. Once Psions/Psaids reach Tier III, they can unleash some pretty terrifying effects even without Mega-Attributes. For now, look at the stuff Novas can already do and Psions/Psiads can potentially do at Psi 6+ then apply that to Talents.<br /> <br /> I suspect that we'll see Tier III Talents in Adventure once it's released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:36:15-08:00","id":1350226,"title":"","content":"I think with Aberrants being able to very imperfectly and brutally imitate psionic modes in Aeon, it's reasonable that a really powerful and advanced flux user could step on the toes of the other two types as long as it fits with the general theme of enhancement through probability/reality/time/etc. I do think reality warping at the highest levels would make sense and wouldn't step on nova toes as long as it feels different. But I also get the impression that flux is harder to use than quantum or psi, so it makes since that talents will be a bit behind psions and novas on what they can at any given point of advancement.<br /> <br /> I'd generally say that flux effects should be less visually flashy than nova powers and less traditionally &quot;psychic&quot; than psionic powers, but I think a powerful flux user should be able to fake those with a little added sleight of hand and trickery, such as using flux to mess with existing energy sources to make them flare up dramatically. So, basically, less like Superman or Luke Skywalker and more like Harry Houdini.<br /> <br /> But I also think it's entirely plausible that a powerful flux user could summon energy from another universe or something like that. Basically, at sufficiently high power level, I think any source could do anything. In general play, though, I'd limit flux like I mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T15:52:33-08:00","id":1350333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350204#post1350204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd stop short of full-on reality manipulation. That said, stepping on toes shouldn't be as much of a concern. Except for specific effects like the Telepathy and Clairsentience Aptitudes, Novas can do anything Psions/Psiads can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I mean.. and we haven't seen the high end stuff Novas may no longer have any of the Time manipulation powers(having been pulled out for paramorphs only)<br /> <br /> <br /> I am ok with there being alot of crossover in the circles but Psions and psiads do look different than novas. So how do you make a &quot;Paramorph God&quot; look different than a nova?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T16:28:13-08:00","id":1350338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350333#post1350333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am ok with there being alot of crossover in the circles but Psions and psiads do look different than novas. So how do you make a &quot;Paramorph God&quot; look different than a nova?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the simplest way would be to play up the incredible luck and odd coincidences aspect instead of blatant displays of superhuman power. It'd probably be achieved via multiple levels of Enhancement at various tasks; and if they've got a sufficient level of Enhancement on a non-opposed task, they don't even need to try, they succeed via Storyteller fiat.<br /> <br /> For example: They need to break into a residential building with a doorman. They've easily got enough 'mojo' to do so, so the Storyteller lets them just walk in the front door while a resident walks out and the doorman is distracted by a bike messenger passing in the other direction. This sort of thing can happen to regular people, but happens to the Paramorph God multiple times every day.<br /> <br /> Done properly, the player should almost never have to actually roll for anything. Their actions are almost guaranteed to achieve at least a minimal degree of success, which actions taken against them either fail outright or only achieve the minimum possible level of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T16:33:33-08:00","id":1350339,"title":"","content":"The Paramorph God doesn't have anything that changes what he <i>is</i>; only what he <i>does</i>. Nothing about growing wings or being covered in scales, etc. Even powers associated with Intention (that is, the higher-power equivalent of Attribute-based Aptitude Gifts) don't really change the character's nature; they just enhance what the attributes let the character do. Though in the case of the Resistance Attributes, that can be a fine line. <br /> <br /> Every power a Paramorph can have should be rooted in Luck, Skill, or Intention: Luck expands to interacting with the Continuum, which includes forward, backward, and sideways in time. Skill involves training: Powers associated with skill involved taking what a skill can normally do to ridiculous levels. Intention involves drive and discipline. They are the most like the powers that a Superior would have, with the main difference being that the attribute in question still involves the character's drive backing it up. <br /> <br /> The ultra-Talent shouldn't have any powers (other than the Luck-based ones) that manipulate their environment; and the ones that they have that affect themselves should be rooted in enhancing what they do rather than what they are (with the aforementioned caveat about Resistance Attributes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-22-2019, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T17:01:24-08:00","id":1350347,"title":"","content":"I would also point to some of the early versions of Wonder Woman as an example of a third-tier Paramorph. As originally conceived, Diana was not a goddess or a demigoddess; she was an Amazon. And the Amazons were not inherently superhuman. Rather, they had access to super science and advanced one might even say superhuman training. Wonder Woman was able to pull off the remarkable feats that she managed because of that training, which was described as channeling mental energy through her body to enhance it.<br /> <br /> It's very reminiscent of stuff that we normally associate with the lights of crouching tiger Hidden dragon, but without the Eastern flavor. That's why I always point to exalted as an example of higher tier paramorphs, at least where skill is concerned. It draws from the same kinds of sources.<br /> <br /> That said, \u201cchi bolts\u201d like those featured in Street Fighter or manifesting weapons composed of <s>Essence</s>Flux is probably a bridge too far \u2014 though in the latter case, I could see a luck based power that lets you summon the proper gear for the task at hand from an alternate reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-22-2019, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T17:13:11-08:00","id":1350348,"title":"","content":"What would a Tier III Talent look like? Get Mage: The Awakening and look at the stuff you can do with Fate magic. Or just build them with any Sphere with the stipulation that they never suffer Paradox but cannot do any &quot;vulgar&quot; effect, only coincidental magic. <br /> <br /> And for more ideas, try to find/watch a series from the 90s called Strange Luck: <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0112182/?ref_=nm_knf_i3\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0112182/?ref_=nm_knf_i3</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T18:05:44-08:00","id":1350358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350348#post1350348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a Tier III Talent look like? Get Mage: The Awakening and look at the stuff you can do with Fate magic. Or just build them with any Sphere with the stipulation that they never suffer Paradox but cannot do any &quot;vulgar&quot; effect, only coincidental magic. <br /> <br /> And for more ideas, try to find/watch a series from the 90s called Strange Luck: <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0112182/?ref_=nm_knf_i3\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0112182/?ref_=nm_knf_i3</a></div> </div> </div> </div>If you want the Luck-based stuff to have a mystical flavor to it, then you could do worse than to base it on MtAw's Fate and Time Arcana; and I'd throw in a bit from Spirit, too, limited to \u201cinteracting with the Shadow\u201d and reskinning &quot;the Shadow\u201d as \u201calternate timelines\u201d.<br /> <br /> Also: Vulgar vs. Coincidental is an Ascension thing, not an Awakening thing \u2014 at least, as of MtAw2e: you still get Paradox, but now it's cause by overreaching with your magic rather than by some sort of blatant vs. subtle divide. <br /> <br /> Besides: higher-tier paramorphs don't necessarily have to have subtle effects. I can definitely see potential for higher-tier paramorphs to pull off flashy stunts that would flat-out break suspension of disbelief if an audience is expecting them to be baselines: Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon with its wirework should be a source of inspiration for Skill-based higher-tier Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-22-2019, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T20:00:19-08:00","id":1350373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350204#post1350204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that we'll see Tier III Talents in Adventure once it's released.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend against holding your breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T20:21:08-08:00","id":1350377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350373#post1350373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would recommend against holding your breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really planning to. Even if such a things were going to happen... it would take a while. Right now Trinity Core exists as a physical book. As does Aeon. Unless somebody's printed it themselves, Aeon Expansion only exits as a digital file. Aberrant isn't even out the door yet and probably won't be for quite some time. And in the middle of all that somebody's wondering, &quot;Hey, when will a product for this third game come to answer some fairly esoteric questions of Talents?&quot; Figure don't hold your breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T20:33:32-08:00","id":1350379,"title":"","content":"I think part of Ian's point is that the higher-tier stuff for Talents isn't going to be part of TC:A! at all: not the core book, not any of its supplements. If higher-tier stuff for paramorphs ever shows up in the Trinity Continuum official publications, it's going to be in some other setting than Adventure!.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T23:06:03-08:00","id":1350396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350347#post1350347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also point to some of the early versions of Wonder Woman as an example of a third-tier Paramorph. As originally conceived, Diana was not a goddess or a demigoddess; she was an Amazon. And the Amazons were not inherently superhuman. Rather, they had access to super science and advanced one might even say superhuman training. Wonder Woman was able to pull off the remarkable feats that she managed because of that training, which was described as channeling mental energy through her body to enhance it.<br /> <br /> It's very reminiscent of stuff that we normally associate with the lights of crouching tiger Hidden dragon, but without the Eastern flavor. That's why I always point to exalted as an example of higher tier paramorphs, at least where skill is concerned. It draws from the same kinds of sources.<br /> <br /> That said, \u201cchi bolts\u201d like those featured in Street Fighter or manifesting weapons composed of <s>Essence</s>Flux is probably a bridge too far \u2014 though in the latter case, I could see a luck based power that lets you summon the proper gear for the task at hand from an alternate reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is some form of exalt covers able to do a whole bunch of things from punch people into Ducks to transform into cities. Even limiting to solars there's a point where they've moved beyond &quot;merely&quot; being good at something to forcing reality to bend to your will in certain defined ways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T00:51:35-08:00","id":1350402,"title":"","content":"Yes; but those \u201ccertain defined ways\u201d are defined in terms of the skills. My point above about \u201cchi bolts\u201d and so on was that only a subset of Exalted's Charms are suitable inspiration for higher-tier Gifts: I could see higher-tier Aim Gifts emulating Solar Archery Charms such as Wise Arrow (the projectiles' paths bend through the air to bypass obstacles between the shooter and his target), Sight Without Eyes (you can accurately shot while literally blindfolded), Force Without Fire (the projectile you fire knocks the target down at the cost of inflicting less damage), Fiery Arrow Attack (the projectile acts as an incendiary round even if it isn't one), There Is No Wind (you get to ignore non-visual conditions such as wind and weather when shooting), and so on; but Phantom Arrow Technique is out, as are Immaculate Golden Bow, Rain of Feathered Death, Solar Spike, Heart-Eating Incineration, etc. <br /> <br /> Basically, as a first draft I'd allow Aim to get everything that Solar Archery Charms permit (assuming they're suitable for the weapon being fired) except for the ones that let you manifest a weapon or projectiles out of nothing. Yes, some of the Charms that I'd allow amount to a limited sort of reality manipulation. That's fine, because of the limits; more on that below. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, a number of the Archery Charms are tied to specific Exalted mechanics (such as the difference between a withering attack and a decisive attack) which may not have counterparts in the Storypath system. It can be hard at times; but I'd want to translate the underlying concept of a given Charm rather than the specific mechanics; and if this makes several different Charms translate into the same Gift or results in some Charms not translating at all, then so much the better: while I like the stuff in the Solar Charms in principle, I find the implementation to be overwrought and a bit too crunchy for my taste. I'd want the uber-Talent counterpart to be more streamlined and intuitive. <br /> <br /> But getting back to my earlier point, note that while Exalted's Archery is about ranged attacks, there are no Charms for it that let you just look at the target and have him burst into flame. You must always wield a bow and use it to shoot an arrow: the Archery skill isn't merely a prerequisite that you must satisfy before you can acquire a given Charm; it's an integral part of the way that Charm works. In a similar way, Skill-based Gifts for all Paramorph tiers should not just require you to learn the appropriate Skills; their use should in some way be extensions of said Skills. Skill-based Gifts cannot duplicate Quantum Powers or Psi Modes that aren't extensions of Skill use; Attribute-based Gifts similarly need to be extensions of your Attributes (which is why I say that they'd be similar to the powers of Superiors). And Luck-based Gifts have to be explained in terms of manipulating time (albeit in the more versatile context of the Continuum, where access to alternate timelines definitely counts as manipulating time): you cannot use a Luck-based Gift to shoot fireballs out of your hands or to float in midair, since those have nothing to do with manipulating time. <br /> <br /> And if you can't justify a given power as Luck-based, Skill-based, or Attribute-based, then a Talent can't have it, regardless of tier. <br /> <br /> Put more prosaically, everything that a Talent can do ultimately comes down to fortune, training, or raw determination. In the latter two cases, Flux merely extends the scope of what would otherwise be possible \u2014 maybe in reality-bending ways; but always building on the foundations provided by the skills and attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T02:54:30-08:00","id":1350413,"title":"","content":"I think we have a hint of possible effects of a Higher Talent on the Inspiration description, it\u2019s about Intention, Skill and Luck. When I first read it, I was expecting some Intention Gifts, but they never come...<br /> <br /> Skill and Luck are prety straight forward, higher effects on skills, maybe higher scale on skill results (mega skill stile), extra dice, better use of momentum, better source of momentum, things like that. In a way it\u2019s all about the Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> Intention is a bit trickier, for a talent it\u2019s about Destructive facet, but it can be more... magic-ish. Maybe flux manipulation (Kamehamehaaaaaaa), time manipulation (speed, time stop, etc), dimension jump (cross time travel, summoning creatures or energies from other dimensions), teleport (in the space-time idea), maybe other weird effects like precognition, and other things that can be explained as seeing thru time, conducting the events to the expected result, changing locally the flux of time, things like that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-23-2019, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T21:46:30-08:00","id":1350579,"title":"","content":"There's a broader point about Esoteric Techniques from Wuxia and how they might or might not be accessable(honestly just putting them into a sort of QK equivalent might work there) How much a Flux should allow someone to Macguyer is pretty much the ultimate point here. Being so good at shooting you can make a gun out of flux is you are saying out, but.. what about being so awesome with guns that you can shoot a rubber band and kill Novas? can I aim carefully placed bursts of wind to strike someone... etc.<br /> <br /> The bigger issue is how much you can macguyver with say Science. Should Tier 3 Talents be able to say build an infinity Gauntlet in a cave? Or a Sonic Screwdriver in an abandoned foundary in 21st century London... how much should they need outside requirements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T00:11:43-08:00","id":1350594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350579#post1350579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a broader point about Esoteric Techniques from Wuxia and how they might or might not be accessable(honestly just putting them into a sort of QK equivalent might work there) How much a Flux should allow someone to Macguyer is pretty much the ultimate point here. Being so good at shooting you can make a gun out of flux is you are saying out, but.. what about being so awesome with guns that you can shoot a rubber band and kill Novas? can I aim carefully placed bursts of wind to strike someone... etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cWhile designing your own Gifts, it's important to remember that Gifts save time and affect the drama of the game and do not simply improve a character's ability to do something.\u201d TC p.196. That said, it then goes on to contrast Gifts to Skill Tricks, which <i>can</i> improve your ability: they can increase your dice pool, change your effective Scale, change the target number, or give you a free stunt. Esoteric Techniques should be able to do either; they're at least as much amped-up Skill Tricks as they are amped-up Gifts. On the other hand, Skill Tricks don't let you flat-out increase the damage of an attack; and I don't think that Esoteric Techniques should, either. Rather than increasing damage, I could see Esoteric Techniques that let you disarm a target or temporarily disabled a limb \u2014 though I figure that such effects should be based on how much damage the attack would normally do; so shooting a rubber band to do pretty much <i>anything</i> effective is probably out. <br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, there's a Gift in the upcoming TC:Ab (\u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d) that lets you mitigate Scale differences. Using it, I could see a normal archer shooting Superman with a regular bow and arrow and actually hurting him. <br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I'd be inclined to give players the option to take an additional Skill Trick above and beyond what his Skill normally permits at the same experience cost as acquiring Gift.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350579#post1350579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger issue is how much you can macguyver with say Science. Should Tier 3 Talents be able to say build an infinity Gauntlet in a cave? Or a Sonic Screwdriver in an abandoned foundary in 21st century London... how much should they need outside requirements?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say that higher-tier Talents should have the same ability to engage in Super-science that psis and novas have: that is, Powered Science is no longer beyond their reach. That said, their inventions should generally follow the same sorts of guidelines as the higher-tier version of Gifts follow: this makes them great an building time machines and the like, and also lets them build inventions that enhance whatever attribute or skill is involved in using said invention. (This is more useful than you might think, as nearly every Skill has associated gear that can be used to enhance the skill's effectiveness.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T15:33:09-08:00","id":1350713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350594#post1350594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the gripping hand, there's a Gift in the upcoming TC:Ab (\u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d) that lets you mitigate Scale differences. Using it, I could see a normal archer shooting Superman with a regular bow and arrow and actually hurting him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I vaguely remember something like that from 1E. During the Aberrant War era, a Hulk expy Aberrant was attacking a military base and no one could stop him. An elderly Adventure! era Daredevil who called himself an Aberrant Hunter showed up in a biplane and proceeded to punch the Hulk guy until he was either knocked out or killed. Every single one of the old guy's punches was a 'Golden BB' attack that bypassed the Aberrant's super durability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T17:50:26-08:00","id":1350933,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I don't have much more to add but I do want to tell you your posts on high level Talents and the ideas you have on taking certain concepts from Exalted is AWESOME. I love reading your posts on that and if you ever decide to actually work on a fan project to say bring that sort of thing to Trinity in a full on mechanical sense you have my attention and my enjoyment. The idea of using Trinity for the idea of Exalted in the modern day would be brilliant. I mean the idea of instead of say N-Day bringing about Novas we have E-Day bringing about super Talents on the level of Solar Exalted would be AWESOME!!!!!! <br /> <br /> So yeah, many thumbs up to you on this awesome idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T19:13:41-08:00","id":1350948,"title":"","content":"I've barely looked at it, but maybe you could consider some of the effects from Scion as possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T08:18:00-08:00","id":1351043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1350594#post1350594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cWhile designing your own Gifts, it's important to remember that Gifts save time and affect the drama of the game and do not simply improve a character's ability to do something.\u201d TC p.196. That said, it then goes on to contrast Gifts to Skill Tricks, which <i>can</i> improve your ability: they can increase your dice pool, change your effective Scale, change the target number, or give you a free stunt. Esoteric Techniques should be able to do either; they're at least as much amped-up Skill Tricks as they are amped-up Gifts. On the other hand, Skill Tricks don't let you flat-out increase the damage of an attack; and I don't think that Esoteric Techniques should, either. Rather than increasing damage, I could see Esoteric Techniques that let you disarm a target or temporarily disabled a limb \u2014 though I figure that such effects should be based on how much damage the attack would normally do; so shooting a rubber band to do pretty much <i>anything</i> effective is probably out.<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, there's a Gift in the upcoming TC:Ab (\u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d) that lets you mitigate Scale differences. Using it, I could see a normal archer shooting Superman with a regular bow and arrow and actually hurting him.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I'd be inclined to give players the option to take an additional Skill Trick above and beyond what his Skill normally permits at the same experience cost as acquiring Gift.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we are not quite on the same page. Esoteric Techiques in Wuxia are the weird shit. Like accupuncturing a biological sex change(actual movie effect) its generally where the &quot;train to do shit that's blatantly magical&quot; resides like Sorcery and Sidereal Martial arts(and some of the celestial level martial arts...) Letting &quot;I train so hard at punching I cna throw energy&quot; fall under a Qk equivalent seems to me allows it to exist but give it some niche protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that higher-tier Talents should have the same ability to engage in Super-science that psis and novas have: that is, Powered Science is no longer beyond their reach. That said, their inventions should generally follow the same sorts of guidelines as the higher-tier version of Gifts follow: this makes them great an building time machines and the like, and also lets them build inventions that enhance whatever attribute or skill is involved in using said invention. (This is more useful than you might think, as nearly every Skill has associated gear that can be used to enhance the skill's effectiveness.) </div> </div> </div>How much does a &quot;Post talent&quot; need tools is what I'm getting at. Should My post Talent in a Cave be Senku from Doctor Stone, or should it be Tony Stark?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T09:44:55-08:00","id":1351061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1351043#post1351043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we are not quite on the same page. Esoteric Techiques in Wuxia are the weird shit. Like accupuncturing a biological sex change(actual movie effect) its generally where the &quot;train to do shit that's blatantly magical&quot; resides like Sorcery and Sidereal Martial arts(and some of the celestial level martial arts...) Letting &quot;I train so hard at punching I cna throw energy&quot; fall under a Qk equivalent seems to me allows it to exist but give it some niche protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> How much does a &quot;Post talent&quot; need tools is what I'm getting at. Should My post Talent in a Cave be Senku from Doctor Stone, or should it be Tony Stark?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even Doctor Strange. What is Dramatic Editing but the alteration of reality on at least an unconscious/unaware level? It's basically magic - a kind of magic (cue Highlander theme from the Immortals thread) anyway. In at least the Marvel universe, magic is a skill, a teachable, learnable skill. Think about what the intersection of Luck, Skill and Aptitude mean at higher levels. Think about magic. A lot of the time magic is about low-probability (but still possible) events managing to to occur. It's technically possible that you could walk through a wall to a room on the other side. Atoms are mostly empty space. If everything lined up just right, you could walk through a wall. Now, it would take trying over the course of a couple of trillion years for that circumstance to occur, but it's possible.<br /> <br /> Novas get their power from Quantum, from the basic physical reality of the universe. Psis get their power from the sub-quantum, perhaps the areas below, above and between the universes. Talents draw their power from other universes, from &quot;quantums&quot; that are filtered and attentuated by their journey to this universe. A Tier III Talent would be able to bolster his connection to that extra-universal power - power drawn from places that might have differing physical laws than this one, allowing them to accomplish feats of something like magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":".  Because English actually is my first/only language and what I write should reflect that. 11-26-2019, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T15:13:47-08:00","id":1351140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1351061#post1351061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or even Doctor Strange. What is Dramatic Editing but the alteration of reality on at least an unconscious/unaware level? It's basically magic - a kind of magic (cue Highlander theme from the Immortals thread) anyway. In at least the Marvel universe, magic is a skill, a teachable, learnable skill. Think about what the intersection of Luck, Skill and Aptitude. Think about magic. A lot of the times magic is about low-probability (but still possible) events to occur. It's technically possible that you could walk through a wall to a room on the other side. Atoms are mostly empty space. If everything lined up just right, you could walk through a wall. Now, it would take trying over the course of a couple of trillion years for that circumstance to occur, but it's possible.<br /> <br /> Novas get their power from Quantum, from the basic physical reality of the universe. Psis get their power from the sub-quantum, perhaps the areas below, above and between the universes. Talents draw their power from other universes, from &quot;quantums&quot; that are filtered and attentuated by their journey to this universe. A Tier III Talent would be able to bolster his connection to that extra-universal power - power drawn from places that might have differing physical laws than this one, allowing them to accomplish feats of something like magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've definately been down the rabbit hole of &quot;Talent becomes Ascension style mage imposing their reality on others&quot; but that seems to kill the whole Psi as magic thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:08:43-08:00","id":1351148,"title":"","content":"That's one reason why I'd limit it primarily to the equivalent of Awakening's Fate and Time Arcana. Paramorphs aren't about tapping into alternate laws of reality; they're about borrowing from alternate histories. They can change the course of events, conjure things, manipulate the flow of time, and eventually even travel through time (where time in the Trinity Continuum can go sideways as well as forward and backward); but fireballs, healing spells, transmutations, mind control, summoning ephemeral entities, and possibly even teleportation is beyond what Luck-based Paramorph powers are capable of (though teleportation might be similar enough to time and dimensional travel to be permitted). <br /> <br /> Let me clarify something, though: as I see it, Luck-based powers are the closest that paramorphs get to what would normally be considered magic: in Exalted terminology, it would be their Sorcery. These are the things that they can learn to do through dedicated training akin to how a magician casts spells or a psiad wields her Aptitudes. <br /> <br /> They certainly should be able to achieve Quantum- or Psi-like results through their Attribute- and Skill-based powers; but those sorts of effects should be channeled through the use of their skills and attributes: you can't just say \u201cI have three dots of Aim, so now I can pick up an Esoteric Technique that lets me shoot laser beams out of my eyes\u201d. Instead, if they're doing something that has a physical effect, they much actually exert themselves physically, in an appropriate manner. If they can attack at a distance without there being a physical projectile, they still need to \u201cthrow\u201d it. If they use a power associated with their medical knowledge to heal someone, they can't just lay their hands on the subject and concentrate for a few seconds; they actually need to <i>use</i> their medical skill. Yes, an Esoteric Technique that changes a person's physical sex is possible (albeit difficult and draining); but it's not done the way a biokinetic would do it, which is to say mostly in the mind; an actual medical procedure would need to be conducted. <br /> <br /> They should also always be better <i>with</i> tools than <i>without</i> them, even if the tools are entirely mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:26:01-08:00","id":1351153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1351140#post1351140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've definitely been down the rabbit hole of &quot;Talent becomes Ascension style mage imposing their reality on others&quot; but that seems to kill the whole Psi as magic thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So kill it. Psi isn't magic. Neither is Quantum. They might have similar effects (both can teleport, both can fly, both generate energy) but how they get there and the scales they tend to use are very different.<br /> <br /> Tier III Talents having the power alter reality is an awesome effect, but it's likely limited by the nature of the Talent. A Nova frying you with a Quantum Blast could potentially apply levels of inhuman Mega-Dexterity to hit you. Even a Psion could apply Psi of 6 or 7 plus mode dots to read/contol your mind, etc. Talents are human. They should stay human. In the World of Darkness Mages are still very much human beings. They might have the &quot;cheat codes&quot; to the universe but they're still human.<br /> <br /> Figure that when a Talent gets to Inspiration 10, he loses all his Gifts, all his facets and his Inspiration is replaced by something else that starts at a 1. Because prior to that moment, Inspiration/Gifts/etc were about how the Talent unconsciously manipulated the universe in subtle ways. Like a sleepwalker who was performing some task, the Talent loses all that unconscious ability and has to learn how to consciously alter the universe. In someway, a Talent reaching this level actually gets de-powered to an extent and has to relearn to do certain things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:46:21-08:00","id":1351197,"title":"","content":"I think I have an idea but I am not sure how to apply it. In Chuubos they have these things called Quest Miracles, for one of the splats broadly it represents training as &quot;Building&quot; so you spend a period of time Building your Technique by training(and various other things but this is the applicable concept). What if something like this functioned for talents(or post Talents) that you had something like Super Science but grows out of EVERY Skill. That way it seems solidly connected still to raw skill but can seem to start simulating more essoteric techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T01:29:34-08:00","id":1351241,"title":"","content":"Reality altering is basically the power of a Talent, they find a parallel reality where it\u2019s possible and make it happen in their reality, that\u2019s one of the ways it is described in Core.<br /> <br /> Now on next step Talent, in Mesia Res we are presented to Mist and super science items that allow the character to travel to parallel realities. As it\u2019s not a nova power or a psi power it\u2019s probably a talent power.<br /> <br /> The items look ancient technology and work as super science, what is very magicish to me. They can use this tech travel to other realities and to bring creatures from other realities. The original idea of some of the items was teleportation, so I would say it\u2019s possible too.<br /> <br /> In Media Res there are other stuffs like super science ghosts too, very interesting.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to add it to your game, but it\u2019s in the game as cannon as it can be.<br /> <br /> What is not in cannon is the manipulation of flux/mist, that is one thing I like to think as possible. Using the cross dimensional properties of the mist it\u2019s possible to create illusions (seeing thru the mist to another dimension where it\u2019s true) and probably cause other kinds of reality altering effects. I like to think that flux itself can be handled, as they use inspiration to power up q-tech (attune and activate), it can be a kind of energy, much like psi, that can be used to other effects, from healing to damage, for example, and maybe even fly. But, as I said, it\u2019s not described as possible anywhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T08:50:10-08:00","id":1351295,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't high-tier paramorphs be able to stack multiple possible, even contradictory outcomes within the same reality? Something like the trick that allows you to 'die' then reappear unscathed, but on a grander scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T09:16:25-08:00","id":1351297,"title":"","content":"I bet a highly focused Talent from a civilization with knowledge of such things could create, lets call it Write, entire worlds, lets for the sake of argument call them Ages, into existence and then use the same ability to transport, lets call it Linking, between them all through a superscience method, which we will call the Art. Just sayin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T09:50:37-08:00","id":1351304,"title":"","content":"I feel like you're making reference to something that I'm missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T09:55:23-08:00","id":1351307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350157-the-limits-of-flux?p=1351304#post1351304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you're making reference to something that I'm missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. Yeah I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Its Myst, Riven, Uru and the D'ni by Cyan Works. In the game an ancient race of man discovered the Art of Writing Ages which basically lets them create worlds that can be visited from the Void that lies between. Its one of those things that I very much see the Trinity Continuum rules being perfect for, especially Talents but also potentially Superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:17:51-08:00","id":1351323,"title":"","content":"I am also assuming there could be NonTalent Paramorphs like how Psiads, Psions and Mesmerists seem to be slightly separate things. And Superiors and Novas definately are. So Tier Three Paramorphs don't have be transcendent Talents. Or there could be a whole line of artifical tier 2s...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T12:17:01-08:00","id":1351340,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there can be some variation at higher Tiers, probably varying from era to era. For instance, I could see mage-like paramorphs in an era that doesn't have any psis in it. For the most part, though, I've been thinking of \u201cdifferent kinds of paramorphs\u201d in terms of the Luck/Skill/Intention split established in TC; and I've been approaching it from the angle that all three are available to all paramorphs: if there are different types, they're distinguished in terms of which areas they find easier, not which areas are available. <br /> <br /> My own attention has mainly been focused on Esoteric Techniques (the Skill-based side of things) because it's both highly versatile and very distinct: the Luck-based side of things is akin to Psi Aptitudes or Quantum Powers in their feel, while the Intention-based side of things overlaps heavily with Superiors and \u201cDark Star\u201d Novas (see my earlier post about Wonder Woman as a paramorph, who I figure would be heavy on the Intention-based side of things along with some Esoteric Techniques like being able to defend against bullets, and having a few paramorph-crafted gadgets like her Lasso of Truth and the healing Purple Ray she had access to back on Paradise Island). But yeah; you could easily have a higher-tier paramorph who focuses exclusively on the Luck-based stuff (Hexes?) and/or the Intention-based stuff (Empowerments?) and who doesn't have a single Esoteric Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T14:13:46-08:00","id":1351358,"title":"","content":"Margaret Weiss and Tracey Hickman wrote a fantasy series titled &quot;The Death Gate Cycle&quot; that dealt with two groups of people with probability bending powers on the scale of Marvel's Scarlet Witch. Some of that stuff may be relevant. I especially liked the way one character got around the series' 'don't raise the dead' prohibition by putting a guy into a sort of Schrodinger's Cat state where he couldn't be killed, but couldn't kill anyone else either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T20:20:35-08:00","id":1352943,"title":"","content":"So with access to Mummy the Curse 2e and its whole non-linear nature of Arisen existence I totally could see Max Mercer and such being in a situation very much like the Arisen - just with a bit less 'curse'. Thinking about it the whole idea for high tier Talents of a particular form is that they can appear backwards and forwards and sideways in time - appearing when needed before dissapearing again after having helped or completed a goal. <br /> <br /> To be honest at some point in the future I will probably take certain idea sections from Mummy the Curse, like chapter 7 with its whole descent adventure seeds, and apply it to Trinity rules and setting. At this time I would use either Superiors or Talents, though other Inspired types might also be permissible depending on what we get from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T01:59:18-08:00","id":1352972,"title":"","content":"That's not a bad connection to make. I wouldn't say that those are the limits of Flux, though; if anything, being \u201cunstuck in time\u201d where you live for a few decades in one era before being uprooted and deposited in another era by something beyond your control strikes me as a valid <i>first step</i> for the time travel capabilities of paramorphs. There ought to come a point where you can control when you jump, and at least have some say as to what your destination will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T06:09:42-08:00","id":1352994,"title":"","content":"I just started watching the 3rd season of Man in the High Castle, and they introduce people able to travel between realities. No time travel, however. So, I'd probably peg them as either Tier 2 with a powerful Gift or just barely Tier 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}